# T-2110 resolved in S-1014 via ground_typevalue_of alternative (eval.rs).
# builtin-type-of now returns TypeValue.Repr for primitive values (Int, Float, String).
# builtin-has-key? "Repr" auto-unpacks the Variant payload via require_dict, producing
# a dict with key "repr" (lowercase). "Repr" (uppercase) is absent → Int(0) for all three.
# The expected output remains Int(0) for all — require_dict payload-unpack + case mismatch.
[
  int-repr:    [builtin-has-key? "Repr" [builtin-type-of 42]]
  float-repr:  [builtin-has-key? "Repr" [builtin-type-of 1.5]]
  string-repr: [builtin-has-key? "Repr" [builtin-type-of "hello"]]
]
=== out
Dict({"int-repr": Int(0), "float-repr": Int(0), "string-repr": Int(0)})
